[{"id":"areset-order","itemId":"asynchronous-reset","role":"core","promptHtml":"In <code class=\"nobreak\">resets</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> is 1 and so is <code class=\"nobreak\">q_async</code>. Then <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_async</code> pulses for 2 ns between two rising edges, while <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync</code> stays 0. Put in order what happens.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>posedge rst_async</code> is in the event list, so the block runs the moment the reset rises and <code class=\"nobreak\">q_async</code> becomes 0 at once, without the clock (lesson 2.3). It stays 0 after the pulse, because nothing runs the block again until the next rising edge; there <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_async</code> is 0, so <code class=\"nobreak\">q_async</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>. If you waited for the rising edge before clearing <code class=\"nobreak\">q_async</code>, you treated it as a synchronous reset, and a synchronous reset would never have seen this pulse at all.</p>","type":"order","steps":["`rst_async` goes to 1, 1 ns after a falling edge of `clk`.","`q_async` becomes 0.","`rst_async` goes back to 0, 2 ns later.","The next rising edge of `clk` arrives.","`q_async` takes `d` again, and becomes 1."],"shuffled":[0,2,3,4,1]},{"id":"areset-find-bug","itemId":"asynchronous-reset","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"This flip-flop should clear <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> the moment <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> rises, without waiting for the clock. Its testbench fails. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p>The event list has only <code>posedge clk</code>, so the block runs only at rising edges and <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> is looked at only then: a synchronous reset. The testbench's first failure is 1 ns after <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> rises in the middle of a cycle, at 13 ns, where <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> is still 1. Written <code>always_ff @(posedge clk or posedge rst) begin</code>, the block also runs the moment <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> rises, and <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> becomes 0 at once. The <code>if (rst)</code> line is right: it is what makes the reset win over <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>, in both kinds.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-02/areset_bug/areset_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// A flip-flop with an asynchronous reset: q becomes 0 the moment rst","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// rises, without waiting for the clock, and stays 0 while rst is 1. At","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// every other rising edge of clk, q takes d.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"areset_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" rst,   ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// clears q at once","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" d,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" q","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"if","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" (rst) q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"1'b0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"else","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"     q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]],"bugLine":10,"fixLine":"always_ff @(posedge clk or posedge rst) begin"},{"id":"areset-fill-event","itemId":"asynchronous-reset","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">stop_led</code> copies switch <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> to LED <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> at each rising edge. Pressing <code class=\"nobreak\">stop</code> must turn the LED off the moment the button goes down, without waiting for the clock. Type the second event of the event list.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>posedge stop</code> makes the block run the moment <code class=\"nobreak\">stop</code> rises, so the <code>if (stop)</code> line turns the LED off at once: an asynchronous reset with another name (lesson 2.3). Without it, the LED would go off only at the next rising edge. <code class=\"nobreak\">stop_led_tb</code> checks that the LED is off 1 ns after <code class=\"nobreak\">stop</code> rises in the middle of a cycle.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-02/stop_led/stop_led.sv","firstLine":1,"totalLines":14,"before":["// An LED that copies switch d at each rising edge of clk. Pressing stop","// turns it off the moment the button goes down, without waiting for the","// clock, and keeps it off while stop is held.","module stop_led (","  input  logic clk,","  input  logic stop,   // 1 while the stop button is pressed","  input  logic d,      // the switch","  output logic q       // the LED",");"],"blankLine":{"left":"  always_ff @(posedge clk or ","right":") begin"},"after":["    if (stop) q <= 1'b0;","    else      q <= d;","  end","endmodule"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"// An LED that copies switch d at each rising edge of clk. Pressing stop","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// turns it off the moment the button goes down, without waiting for the","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// clock, and keeps it off while stop is held.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"stop_led","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" stop,   ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// 1 while the stop button is pressed","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" d,      ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// the switch","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" q       ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// the LED","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"or","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":") ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]},"after":[[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"if","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" (stop) q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"1'b0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"else","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"      q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]]},"accept":["posedge stop"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"The second event"},{"id":"areset-report-cell","itemId":"asynchronous-reset","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">resets.sv</code> has one flip-flop with each kind of reset. Vivado built it for the Arty A7-100T. Below is the Primitives table of its Utilization report: one row for each kind of cell, with how many the design uses.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">q_async</code> has the asynchronous reset, so it needs a flip-flop that can clear without the clock: the FDCE, whose CLR input does that (lesson 2.3). The FDRE row is <code class=\"nobreak\">q_sync</code>, whose R input acts only at a rising edge. IBUF and OBUF are the pins, and BUFG is the clock.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/resets/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":179,"excerpt":["8. Primitives","-------------","","+----------+------+---------------------+","| Ref Name | Used | Functional Category |","+----------+------+---------------------+","| IBUF     |    4 |                  IO |","| OBUF     |    2 |                  IO |","| FDRE     |    1 |        Flop & Latch |","| FDCE     |    1 |        Flop & Latch |","| BUFG     |    1 |               Clock |","+----------+------+---------------------+"],"ask":"Type the Ref Name of the cell Vivado used for q_async.","answer":"FDCE","numeric":false}]